  <header class="surface-card rounded-[1.5rem] p-6 sm:p-8"><p class="text-[10px] font-extrabold uppercase tracking-[.18em] text-indigo-200">NEXUS POLICIES</p><h1 class="mt-2 text-3xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-white">Terms of Service & Community Rules</h1><p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-400">Draft for product development. The site owner must supply the legal entity, contact details, age rules, dispute process, and effective date and obtain legal review before launch.</p></header>
  <section class="surface-card prose-nexus mt-4 space-y-5 rounded-[1.4rem] p-5 text-sm leading-7 text-slate-400 sm:p-7">
    <h2 class="text-lg font-extrabold text-white">1. Acceptable use</h2><p>Use Nexus lawfully and respectfully. Do not threaten, harass, stalk, dox, impersonate, defraud, spam, manipulate votes or feeds, evade enforcement, distribute malware, or interfere with service integrity. Do not publish non-consensual intimate imagery, voyeuristic recordings, personal data for harassment, or material that violates others' rights. Do not use the service to facilitate crimes.</p>
    <h2 class="text-lg font-extrabold text-white">2. Accounts and security</h2><p>Protect your sign-in credentials and devices. Do not share passwords, recovery codes, or private encryption keys with support staff or moderators. Tell support promptly if you believe your account is compromised. The operator may limit registrations, rate-limit actions, require verification, or suspend access to protect the service.</p>
    <h2 class="text-lg font-extrabold text-white">3. Content and licenses</h2><p>You retain rights you have in your original content. You grant the operator a non-exclusive, worldwide, limited license to host, store, reproduce, transmit, adapt for technical formats, and display content as needed to operate the service and show it to the audiences you choose. You represent that you have the rights and lawful basis needed to submit content, including media containing other people. Public posts can be copied, indexed, cached, or screenshotted by others and may persist in external systems after you delete them.</p>
    <h2 class="text-lg font-extrabold text-white">4. Moderation and appeals</h2><p>Moderation can include warnings, content labels, removal, thread locks, community restrictions, rate limits, temporary bans, permanent bans, and shadow bans that reduce a user's public visibility. Enforcement should be proportionate, documented, and reviewable. Contact <a href="/support" class="text-indigo-200 hover:text-white">Customer Support</a> to appeal a decision. The operator may preserve relevant records for security, an appeal, legal obligations, or a lawful claim.</p>
    <h2 class="text-lg font-extrabold text-white">5. Private messages</h2><p>Encrypted direct messages are intended to protect message content from routine server and database access. They are not guaranteed anonymity or direct peer-to-peer transport. The service can see message metadata. Recipients can screenshot or copy content, and selected text is disclosed when you report a message. Lost browser encryption keys may make historical messages unrecoverable. Never use this beta implementation for information that requires independently audited high-assurance communications.</p>
    <h2 class="text-lg font-extrabold text-white">6. Reports, safety, and response</h2><p>Use reporting tools honestly. False or abusive reports may violate these terms. The operator can review reported public content and evidence deliberately submitted by users. The site may restrict illegal or harmful content, comply with valid legal process, and preserve records when lawfully required. Nothing in these terms prevents lawful reporting to authorities or the National Privacy Commission.</p>
    <h2 class="text-lg font-extrabold text-white">7. Privacy</h2><p>The separate <a href="/privacy" class="text-indigo-200 hover:text-white">Privacy Notice</a> explains data processing and data subject request options. Please read it before using the service. The operator must keep it accurate as actual hosting providers, purposes, retention rules, and contact details evolve.</p>
    <h2 class="text-lg font-extrabold text-white">8. Availability, liability, and changes</h2><p>The service is supplied on an evolving basis and may be changed, interrupted, or discontinued. To the extent allowed by applicable law, the operator disclaims implied warranties and is not responsible for content posted by users or third-party service outages. These terms do not exclude liability that cannot legally be excluded. Material changes should be announced with a revised effective date.</p>
    <h2 class="text-lg font-extrabold text-white">9. Governing law and contact</h2><p>These terms are intended to be interpreted consistently with applicable laws of the Philippines. The operator should obtain local legal advice on consumer protection, intermediary liability, lawful orders, intellectual property, cybercrime, privacy, and dispute-resolution provisions. Contact: <span class="text-amber-200">[insert operator support address and registered business / person details]</span>.</p>
